166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (As autonomous AI agents proliferate across enterprise workflows, the protocols that govern their communication have become critical infrastructure. The Model Context Protocol \(MCP\), Agent-to-Agent \(A2A\), and Agent Communication Protocol \(ACP\) have each emerged as foundational standards for connecting agents to tools and to one another. Yet all three share a fundamental architectural weakness: they require trusted intermediaries to see the data in transit. API servers, cloud relays, and proxy gateways sit in the path of every message, creating honeypots of sensitive information and single points of compromise.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (This paper presents an alternative architecture, implemented in the open-source Pembrook project, that layers JSON-RPC 2.0 messaging over atRPC on the atPlatform \(built on the atPlatform Protocol by Atsign\). This approach delivers end-to-end encryption, cryptographic identity, and zero open inbound ports while remaining fully compatible with the semantics of MCP, A2A, and ACP. The result is a system where the infrastructure operators themselves, including the atPlatform relay, are cryptographically prevented from reading the data that flows through them. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
