/E (Every participant in the atPlatform Protocol, whether a person, device, or AI agent, is represented by a unique identifier called an Atsign \(e.g.,              ,              ,                    \). Each Atsign owns a pair of asymmetric cryptographic keys \(RSA 2048 or ECC\). )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 685 0 R
/E (The private keys are generated and stored exclusively on the edge device; they never traverse the network. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 686 0 R
/E (The public keys are made globally available through the atPlatform Protocol so that any participant can verify identity and establish encrypted channels. Authentication uses PKAM \(Public Key Authentication Method\), which is cryptographic rather than token-based. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (Unlike OAuth tokens, which can be stolen and replayed, Atsign authentication requires proof of possession of a private key.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
